WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.599 --> 00:00:03.429
Away from China’s bustling cities,

00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:06.470
a crisis is mounting in rural areas

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.820
that will impact the entire country.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.270
By the time China’s children reach working age,

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:14.600
⅓ of them will be intellectually stunted.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.540
In rural China, 50% of 8th graders

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.860
score below 90 on IQ tests.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.920
According to the 2010 census,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.580
only 24% of China's labor force attended high school.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.030
With China’s booming economy placing new demands

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.279
on its workers, economist Scott Rozelle asks:

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:35.539
“ What do you do with 400 million people

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.260
in your labor force who can’t learn?

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.700
"That can't switch jobs?"

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.710
"This problem of healthy cognitive development,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.680
especially among China’s rural population,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.300
which is about 60-70% of its babies,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.440
is the biggest problem that China faces

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.440
that no one knows about.”

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.280
To tackle this problem, Rozelle established

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.100
collaborations with researchers

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.360
and institutional partners to form:

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.720
The group first tried to boost test scores

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.620
by improving children’s health.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.520
They conducted surveys in rural areas

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.850
and found that 27% of children were anemic,

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.120
which is an indicator of malnutrition,

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.500
37% had intestinal worms

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.500
and 20% had myopia.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.640
The researchers realized that any one of these factors

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.530
would obstruct education.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.500
If you’re sick how can you learn?

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.240
REAP provided students with vitamins,

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.700
de-worming treatment, and corrective glasses--

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.140
Sure enough, their math scores improved far more

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.280
than their peers who didn’t receive interventions.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.640
These findings helped convince China’s

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.180
central government to establish

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.380
a school lunch program in 2011

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.700
that now benefits more than

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.370
20 million rural students daily.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.320
There’s a giant body of evidence showing that

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.840
it's the first 1000 days that sets the stage for later

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.110
educational achievement and adult health.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.820
So, Rozelle’s team started focusing on children

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.640
in the earliest stages of life.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.720
In 2013, they tested 1800 babies

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.750
from 348 villages in impoverished areas

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.510
of the Qinling Mountain Region.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:17.170
49% were anemic and 29% scored below normal

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.510
on a standard intelligence assessment for babies

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.320
called the Bayley Test.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.030
But this time, when the team intervened with vitamins,

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.040
test scores didn’t improve.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.240
They're entering a time when they should be

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.400
starting to learn other things but with

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.640
very low levels of cognition.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.040
That’s when Rozelle turned to parenting

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.020
as the possible culprit.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:41.880
In 2014, REAP started asking caregivers how
they parented.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.610
Just a ⅓ reported playing with or singing to their child,

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:49.420
11% had told a story to their child the previous day,

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:52.500
and less than 5% had read to their child.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.780
REAP then studied 513 child/caregiver pairs.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.660
Half received in-home parental training,

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.400
which involved weekly coaching for 6 months.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.690
The study found that the training brought Bayley scores

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:07.140
up to normal but only when the mother was present.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.460
With many mothers leaving

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.720
rural homes to find jobs in cities,

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.420
30% to 40% of rural children are raised by grandma.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.480
When a grandmother received

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.870
the in-home training however,

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.200
the child’s Bayley score barely budged.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.660
The trainers had trouble reaching the children

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.830
and their mothers in these remote regions

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.960
and the process was time-consuming and expensive.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.140
The in-home visits did little to relieve

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.560
the isolation of kids,

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.720
whose mothers weren’t in the picture.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.510
What’s more, a questionnaire filled out by the mothers

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.660
who did remain with their children suggests

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.220
40% of them showed signs of depression.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.220
To overcome these obstacles REAP has embarked

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.700
on its most ambitious experiment yet.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.750
The team has targeted 100 villages in

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.690
The Qinling Mountain Region and set up

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:55.640
early childhood education centers in half of them.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.310
There’s free play, group activities, reading,

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.740
and one-one parent training.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.700
They are following 1200 baby/caregiver pairs

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.740
to see how a stimulating environment

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.340
and effective parenting

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.950
shape the intelligence of young children.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.270
“ We went in one generation from everyone raising

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.229
who they thought were to be subsistence farmers

00:04:17.229 --> 00:04:19.920
and now we need to raise college kids.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.870
And that’s true in Latin America,

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.160
it's true in other middle-income countries.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.180
Unless you get zero to three right

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:31.540
there’s going to be huge huge problems.”

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.740
The first assessment of the childhood

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.960
education centers will be completed in early 2018.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.460
If their interventions are successful,

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.340
Rozelle and his team hope to convince

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.460
Chinese authorities to scale up

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.120
and establish early education centers nationwide.

